# The `hidden<Tab>test` cheat and the super jackpot value on DRAGON with the real DragonRules. The engine owns
# `hidden<Tab>test` on FT tables (a state machine over upper-case VKs: Tab, not space; engine_diff C5). Expected values
# are literals. The game starts at frame 0: the engine's Reset sets SuperJackpotScore = 20000 (FT 0x402) and the rules'
# NewGame (dragon_rules.cpp, TableControlHandler new-game case: `control::TableG->SuperJackpotScore = 2500000`, FT value)
# runs right after it, so frame 20 pins the rules' value 2,500,000. The Reset value 20000 is only observable with the
# test-only stub rules: IU3b_rules_dragon.uh frame 60 (`super_jackpot == 20000`, player 2 starts with the Reset value).
init window 960 666
init fixed_dt 10
init seed 1
2 key down new_game
3 key up new_game
# Reset leaves the third accumulator at 20000 (FT Reset 0x402); the rules' NewGame then sets 2,500,000.
20 expect super_jackpot == 2500000
20 expect n_cheat == 0
# "hidden test" with a space is not the FT sequence: cheat mode stays off.
30 type hidden\stest
70 expect n_cheat == 0
# A wrong key in the middle resets the machine.
80 type hiddxn\ttest
120 expect n_cheat == 0
# The real sequence turns cheat mode on.
130 type hidden\ttest
170 expect n_cheat == 1
# Upper-case input is the same sequence (VKs): typing it again keeps the mode on (FT sets, it does not toggle).
180 type HIDDEN\tTEST
220 expect n_cheat == 1
230 quit
